WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
The chief executive has got
to be bold within reason

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.570
and daring in application.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:08.940
I recognize very
few people watching

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.980
this will become president.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.800
But I think you'll find
lessons in leadership that

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.940
will apply to your life.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.040
As president, sometimes
I had information

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.600
that the American
people didn't know.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.225
And therefore, I had
to make decisions,

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:28.320
what was best for the
country, on knowledge

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.340
that wasn't evident.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.260
That's just the
nature of leadership.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.050
So long as you're
guided by principle

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.490
and so long as you're guided
by a cause greater than self,

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:39.930
you can endure criticism.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.692
Because it's gonna come.

00:00:41.692 --> 00:00:43.650
One of the things I missed
after the presidency

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.210
was this daily learning.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.333
And, thankfully, painting
came into my life.

00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:49.500
It's a learning experience
because, with every paint

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.295
stroke, you learn something new.

00:00:51.295 --> 00:00:52.920
All right, I'm gonna
do another flower.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.740
It's important to have a set
of priorities that guide you.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:59.130
And your team, your
company, your managers,

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.960
have got to understand
those priorities.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.880
To me, the most
important priorities

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.880
were my faith and my
family and my friends.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.250
That may sound corny
to some, but it

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.470
helps you reorganize
the rest of your life.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.177
Welcome darling.

00:01:11.177 --> 00:01:11.760
LAURA: Thanks.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:12.260
Great.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.952
Glad to be here.

00:01:13.952 --> 00:01:15.660
GEORGE: When I was
speaking to audiences,

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:18.510
I didn't want them to think
I was smarter than they were.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.580
One of the keys to
communication is

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.710
to figure out how to
enable the person you're

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.090
talking to to relax.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:27.030
You know, I was a
master at the malaprop.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:28.620
Misunderestimate.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.120
The press corps reaction
was, "Did the guy really

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:32.960
just say that?"

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.850
[CHUCKLES]

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:37.910
I remember, right after
9/11 in the Oval Office,

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:40.100
talking about
praying for families

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.080
that had suffered loss.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.520
I broke down in tears.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.590
If your heart is
touched, let people know

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:47.450
that your heart is touched.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:49.040
Not everybody is
gonna be a leader,

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.560
but everybody can end up
being a better person.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.540
The challenge of
life is not to attain

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:56.210
wealth and status and power.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:58.700
The challenge of
life is to improve

00:01:58.700 --> 00:01:59.990
and to learn to love better.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:02.840
And everybody can do that.

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:08.540
I'm George W. Bush, and
this is MasterClass.

